<p>Image:</p>

<p>The Mandan Historical Society shutdown the downtown museum space in the NP Beanery in August 2011 after its lease was cancelled by the Mandan Progress Organization.Materials were moved; split between private storage. A small display area was offered in their by members of the ND Railroad Museum in north Mandan after the Steele depot was moved to their facility in October 2011. New displays were constructed and materials moved to the current NDSRR museum "freight house" building after it was completed in 2018. Our displays have already outgrown the 560 sq ft of our current space. We repeatedly turn down additions to our collection due to limited space. Based on our recent experience with our museum operation, our strategic plan envisions the next location with a building with at least 1200 sq ft of floor space. The Board of Directors hopes to establish an exploratory committee soo to indentify potential funds and explore our next opportunity.</p>

<p>Exhibits require a commitment of both money and volunteer time. Please help us with a contribution of either your time or financial support. Contact us info@mandanhistory.org</p>

